title: Refactor the preimage pallet to use fungible traits
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: "## Overview\n\nThis PR migrates the preimage pallet from the deprecated\
    \ `Currency`/`ReservableCurrency` traits to the modern `fungible` traits (via\
    \ `Consideration`), as part of the umbrella tracking issue #226.\n\nThe preimage\
    \ pallet was already ~80% migrated: it used `Consideration` + `HoldReason` for\
    \ all **new** deposit operations. However, `type Currency: ReservableCurrency`\
    \ was still in the Config trait (marked `// TODO#1569: Remove.`) solely to support\
    \ a lazy migration (`do_ensure_updated`) that converted old `StatusFor` entries\
    \ on every access.\n\nThis PR replaces that lazy migration with a proper `SteppedMigration`\
    \ and removes all `Currency`-related code.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Removed from Config\
    \ trait**: `type Currency: ReservableCurrency<Self::AccountId>`\n- **Removed `StatusFor`\
    \ storage item**: the old-format storage map (v0/v1 era)\n- **Removed `OldRequestStatus`\
    \ enum** from lib.rs (moved to migration module)\n- **Removed `ensure_updated`\
    \ extrinsic** (call_index 4): was a user-callable dispatchable for triggering\
    \ lazy migration\n- **Removed `do_ensure_updated` function** and all 7 inline\
    \ calls to it throughout the pallet\n- **Removed error variants** `TooMany` and\
    \ `TooFew` (only used by `ensure_updated`)\n- **Removed** `BalanceOf<T>` type\
    \ alias and `MAX_HASH_UPGRADE_BULK_COUNT` constant\n- **Bumped storage version**\
    \ from 1 to 2\n\n## Migration: `LazyMigrationV1ToV2`\n\nThe migration (`pallet_preimage::migration::v2::LazyMigrationV1ToV2<T,\
    \ OldCurrency>`) uses multi-block stepped execution via the `SteppedMigration`\
    \ trait:\n\n- **Multi-block**: Processes `StatusFor` entries one at a time with\
    \ weight-limited batching, resuming across blocks via cursor\n- **Two-phase per\
    \ entry**: (1) `OldCurrency::unreserve` the old reserved balance, (2) `T::Consideration::new`\
    \ to create a new hold ticket with `HoldReason::Preimage`\n- **Graceful handling**:\
    \ Supports entries in all states \u2014 `Unrequested` with deposits, `Requested`\
    \ with/without deposits\n- **try-runtime support**: `pre_upgrade` counts old entries;\
    \ `post_upgrade` verifies they were all migrated to `RequestStatusFor`\n\nThe\
    \ existing v1 migration was also refactored to accept an `OldCurrency` generic\
    \ parameter (same pattern as the multisig PR #11064), decoupling it from `Config::Currency`.\n\
    \n## Benchmarking\n\n- Replaced `Currency` trait usage with `pallet_balances`\
    \ via `fungible::Mutate::set_balance()` (pallet-balances added as optional dep,\
    \ enabled only by `runtime-benchmarks` feature)\n- Removed `ensure_updated` benchmark\n\
    - Added `v2_migration_step` benchmark covering: old entry setup with `ReservableCurrency::reserve`,\
    \ iterator read, unreserve, consideration creation, and cursor generation\n\n\
    ## Integration\n\nRuntimes must remove `type Currency = Balances;` from their\
    \ `impl pallet_preimage::Config`:\n\n```diff\nimpl pallet_preimage::Config for\
    \ Runtime {\n-   type Currency = Balances;\n    type ManagerOrigin = EnsureRoot<AccountId>;\n\
    \    type Consideration = HoldConsideration<...>;\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nRuntimes\
    \ using `pallet_migrations` (multi-block migrations) should register the new migration:\n\
    \n```rust\ntype Migrations = (\n    // ... existing migrations ...\n    pallet_preimage::migration::v2::LazyMigrationV1ToV2<Runtime,\
    \ Balances>,\n);\n```\n\n## Resources\n\nThis is part of the umbrella task #226.\n\
    \n## TODO\n\n- [ ] Run `try-runtime-cli` against Westend / Westend AH to validate\
    \ migration on live state\n- [ ] Generate proper weights via `/cmd bench`\n- [\
    \ ] Generate prdoc via `/cmd prdoc`\n- [x] Add labels (at minimum `T1-FRAME`)"
